1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,480
Our project studies complete physical pick-and-place with a Franka Panda
in MuJoCo.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:10,640
We investigate blocked approaches, corrupted geometry and contact
retention.

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:15,280
The aim is to explain task failures and test bounded interventions.

4
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:21,720
The baseline loads six public YCB models and supports seeded random
object selection and placement.

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:26,280
This complete run starts with a checked approach and physical finger
closure.

6
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:31,120
Contact lifts and holds the target before the robot begins its transfer.

7
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:36,280
The arm carries the object to the destination, lowers it and opens the
fingers.

8
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:41,280
Release and table support are checked; failures remain in the
evaluation.

9
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:49,200
Mesh-based candidates are proposals. Inverse kinematics and collision
checks decide which can execute.

10
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:56,040
Complete success requires an eighty-millimeter lift, a one-second hold
and sustained bilateral contact.

11
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:01,160
Release must be stable, within fifty-five millimeters of the
destination.

12
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:05,840
Planning still uses simulator geometry; sensing is synthetic.

13
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,720
The original candidates are rejected because a nearby can blocks the
palm.

14
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:17,160
We keep the scene and safety checks, adding bounded inclined and offset
grasp alternatives.

15
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:23,600
The chosen alternative lifts the target and carries it through the
checked corridor.

16
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:31,240
The robot lowers and releases it. This development demonstration is
separate from the paired evaluation.

17
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:37,400
This elastic model genuinely deforms; the YCB foam brick in the baseline
remains rigid.

18
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:43,400
The controller regulates the weaker finger contact to retain the object
during lift and transfer.

19
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:49,600
Fixed preload completes two of six soft-object tasks; regulation
completes six of six.

20
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:55,240
These force and strain curves illustrate one development run, rather
than a group average.

21
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:01,480
Across formal trials, mean peak strain rises from about three-point-
seven to four-point-nine percent.

22
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:07,400
Retention improves within the tested limits; reduced deformation is not
demonstrated.

23
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,960
A separate rigid-load study randomizes mass, friction and actuator
delay.

24
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:17,680
Regulation changes completion from ten of twelve to twelve of twelve.

25
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:24,040
Synthetic depth includes missing stripes, drift, outliers and a
persistent calibration bias.

26
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:29,760
The single-packet method completes six of twelve tasks; naive fusion
completes only one.

27
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:36,200
Cross-packet voxel support rejects transient outliers and reaches nine
successes in twelve trials.

28
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:44,320
This successful development example uses the robust observer, without
target CAD or instance labels in grasp estimation.

29
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:51,160
Planning still uses simulator geometry; measured observations do not
make the entire system vision-only.

30
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:55,520
The robot carries and releases the object in this illustration.

31
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:59,760
The formal failures remain wedge slips, in separate trials.

32
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:04,560
A transient command fault leaves the first closure wider than the
target.

33
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:09,080
No bilateral contact is detected; the grasp is rejected.

34
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:12,640
The robot opens and withdraws safely.

35
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:17,080
It reobserves and makes a second grasp in the same evolving scene.

36
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:22,760
The second grasp holds through lift and transfer; the scene was never
reset.

37
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:27,960
After lowering and release, table support and final placement are
verified.

38
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:33,080
All six controlled episodes recover; broader recovery remains unproven.

39
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:37,840
A passive hinge remains dynamic while the whole assembly is transported.

40
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:43,360
All six assembly tasks succeed; deliberate lid opening is not
demonstrated.

41
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:48,880
Measured points propose grasps for procedural instances without target
CAD.

42
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:53,160
Both methods tie at eleven of twelve, with one shared slip.

43
00:03:53,160 --> 00:04:00,040
In separate stronger-clutter trials, active sensing changes completion
from five of six to three of six.

44
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:04,720
The candidate study contains one hundred eighty paired physical
episodes.

45
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:10,960
With three neighbors, local alternatives change success from fifty-four
to fifty-eight out of sixty.

46
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:16,160
With five neighbors, success changes from twenty-six to twenty-nine out
of thirty.

47
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:22,680
The separate exploratory screening contains one hundred twenty-six
episodes across fourteen conditions.

48
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:29,520
The intervals show substantial uncertainty; none of the comparisons
passes its stated statistical threshold.

49
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:34,000
Initial scenes and physics are paired, with all failures retained.

50
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:39,200
Development demonstrations are excluded from both evaluation
denominators.

51
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:44,760
The main finding is to diagnose geometry, sensing and contact retention
together.

52
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:50,520
Source code, frozen records and the ten-page report provide reproduction
instructions.

53
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:54,120
Forty-nine tests and both evidence audits pass.

54
00:04:54,120 --> 00:05:00,000
Next steps target wedge stability, deformation-aware control and less
ideal sensing.
